// Stealth address derivation: a one time public value is derived from the recipient's
// view key and a sender chosen nonce by absorbing them through the permutation. The
// sender can compute it from public data and the nonce; only the recipient, holding the
// view key, can recognize and later spend to it. This unlinks a payment from the
// recipient's long term address. Run: zkolang shield/stealth_address.zkl
include "hash.zkl";

input view_key;
secret nonce;
output permute(view_key + nonce);
